	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">McDonnell Douglas MD-11 PMDG ou TFDI.</span></span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Boeing 737-Series iFly et PMDG.</span></span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">BAe Jetstream 4100 PMDG.</span></span></span><br />
	<span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">Etc..</span></span></span><br />
	&nbsp;</li>
</ul>

<h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\"><br />
<strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline\">5-LINE OPERATIONS</span></strong></span></span></h2>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;</span><br />
This division allows free flights. Any flight may be carried out with the aircraft and to the destination of choice. No restriction regarding the aircraft change rule at the Orly Hub. Flight hours and PIREPs count toward the VA career. Call sign <strong>ACFxxx</strong> or <strong>ACFxxxx</strong> (3 digits for domestic flights and 4 digits for international flights). Flight plan REMARK section: <strong>OPR/AIR INTER FLIGHT OPR BY AIR CHARTER INTERNATIONAL</strong></span></span></p>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\"><strong>5.0</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Members MUST NOT use their Company ID (e.g., IT001) instead of a flight number; they must either use a random 3- or 4-digit flight number (e.g., ITF756 or ITF2365, 3 digits for domestic flights, 4 digits for international flights), or, if possible, use the specified flight number for the flight (specified in the “Company” tab under “Schedules and Destinations” on the website). In addition, the flight number must change for each flight.<span style=\"color:#000000;\"><br />
&nbsp;</span><br />
The use of a bigram (i.e., initials, e.g., AD for André Dupont, normally specified in the registration confirmation email) is optional and left to the members’ discretion.<br />
<span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;</span><br />
Example of a flight number under IVAO:<br data-end=\"7717\" data-start=\"7714\" />
Flight plan INDICATOR section: <strong>ITF756</strong><br data-end=\"7757\" data-start=\"7754\" />
If using a bigram: Flight plan REMARK section: IT756AD preceded by CALL/ or CALLSIGN/ or INDICATIVE/. Example: <strong>CALL/IT756AD</strong></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: medium\"></span></strong></span><br />
<br />
<strong><span style=\"font-size: medium\">5.1</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: medium\"> -&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Each member agrees to complete at least <strong data-end=\"64\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"50\">one flight</strong> (one PIREP filed and validated) every <strong data-end=\"114\" data-start=\"103\">60 days</strong> in order to maintain <strong data-end=\"160\" data-start=\"136\">active member status</strong>. If no flight is validated within a 60-day period, the member’s status will automatically become <strong data-end=\"270\" data-start=\"258\">inactive</strong>. However, inactive members and/or members set aside from the VA may submit a request to be reinstated to active status (at the discretion of the staff members and subject to the motivation provided by the requesting member).</span></span><br />
&nbsp;</p>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\"><strong>5.1.1</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">A member may request a period of inactivity for personal reasons. Acceptance and duration will depend on the member’s needs.</span></span></p>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><br />
<strong><span style=\"font-size: medium\">5.2</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: medium\"> -&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Flight selection depends on the pilots and their availability (unless otherwise specified in schedules and/or subsidiary/fly-in flights). Pilots MUST perform flights in real-time mode (simulation time = x1) unless unavoidable circumstances beyond their control. PAUSE mode must be AVOIDED on IVAO and VATSIM networks, as well as prolonged absence from the cockpit unless approved by the controller and in accordance with IVAO and VATSIM rules.</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\"></span></span><span style=\"font-size: medium\"><br />
&nbsp;<br />
<strong>5.3</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Members must strive to conduct flights as realistically as possible using all available systems/software/hardware (e.g., real weather/time, MAX simulation difficulty, etc.).</span></span><br />
&nbsp;</p>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\"><strong>5.3.1</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">The time used during a flight will be at the pilot’s discretion, chosen from the following three options:</span><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">&nbsp;</span></span></span></p>

<ul>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\">The user\'s local time&nbsp;</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\">The local time at the location where the flight takes place&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\">&nbsp;</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\">The scheduled flight time</span></span></li>
</ul>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br />
<span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\"><br />
<strong>5.4</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Members are responsible for submitting flight reports via the Operation Control Center - OCC\'s PIREP system (manually or via ACARS).</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\"></span></span><br />
<br />
<strong><span style=\"font-size: medium\">5.5</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: medium\"> -&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">For proper operation of&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">the Operation Control Center - OCC</span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">&nbsp;and realism, it is requested (when possible and depending on the aircraft used) to follow these parameters,&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">please note that the parameters for substitute aircraft (see §6.0) are also included<span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">:</span></span></p>

<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"> </span></span></p>

<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"> </span></span></p>

<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"> </span></span></p>

