<ul>
	<li data-end=\"9512\" data-start=\"9307\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Load factor for all aircraft: per passenger = 83 kg (190 lb) + 3 kg (7 lb) carry-on + 19 kg (42 lb) checked baggage. Aircraft profiles in SIMBRIEF should be set accordingly.</span></span></li>
	<li data-end=\"9565\" data-start=\"9515\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Passenger load factor: 80% for Air Inter flights</span></span></li>
	<li data-end=\"9635\" data-start=\"9568\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Passenger load factor: 100% for Air Charter International flights</span></span></li>
	<li data-end=\"9694\" data-start=\"9638\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Cargo load factor: 80% for Inter Cargo Service flights</span></span></li>
	<li data-end=\"9753\" data-start=\"9697\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Cost Index Airbus A330 = Medium haul 60 / Long haul 30</span></span></li>
	<li data-end=\"9795\" data-start=\"9756\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Cost Index Airbus A319/A320/A321 = 50</span></span></li>
	<li data-end=\"9913\" data-start=\"9798\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Flight altitude = Use optimal altitude for the aircraft type according to route and weight per manuals and charts</span></span></li>
	<li data-end=\"10022\" data-start=\"9916\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Speed = Use speeds calculated from CI or LRC or per aircraft charts. Example: Fokker 100 CI = 40 and LRC</span></span></li>
	<li data-end=\"10238\" data-start=\"10025\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Fueling: The OCC automatically calculates fuel cost from departure airport. Only carry necessary fuel for the flight (complying with regulations). Example: No need to fully tank a Boeing 747-128 for Paris-Nice</span></span></li>
	<li data-end=\"10377\" data-start=\"10241\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Fuel calculation = (Route + 5%) + diversion + expected holding (if known) and/or discretion of Captain + 45 minutes at economic cruise</span></span></li>
</ul>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;<span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\">a) Fokker 100 procedures</span></span></span></span></p>

<ul>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;</span></span>Normal operation with TAY 650-15 engines: Cost Index 40 (for long-haul sectors use CI 24 in climb, then CI 30 in cruise). Use LRC mode.</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">&nbsp;</span>Normal operation with TAY 620-15 engines: Cost Index 24 in climb, then CI 40 in cruise. Use LRC mode.</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;</span></span>Normal takeoff configuration: Flaps 0.</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;</span></span>Flaps 8° takeoff mandatory: after ground de-icing or when required by performance considerations (short or contaminated runway).</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;</span></span>Flaps 15° takeoff mandatory: when a Low Level Windshear (LLWS) advisory is in effect.</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;</span></span>FLEX takeoff permitted, except when a Low Level Windshear (LLWS) advisory is in effect or when required by performance considerations (short or contaminated runway); in these cases, full TO thrust is mandatory.</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;</span></span>During winter operations / cold weather conditions: ECS bleeds set to ECON for the entire flight. Use NORM during the rest of the year.</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;</span></span>Standard landing configuration: Flaps 42°, except when a Low Level Windshear (LLWS) advisory is in effect or when required by performance considerations (short or contaminated runway).</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Flaps 25 landing mandatory: for automatic landings or CAT II/CAT III approaches, when a Low Level Windshear (LLWS) advisory is in effect, or in the event of an engine failure.</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Use IDLE REVERSE only (unless additional reverse thrust is required).</span></li>
</ul>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">&nbsp;<span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\">b) Aircraft Parameters</span></span></span></p>

<p>Go to \"The Training center\" then \"Aircraft Parameters\" or clic <a href=\"articles.php?lng=en&amp;pg=6069&amp;mnuid=5412&amp;tconfig=0#z2\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000cc;\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\"><strong>HERE</strong></span></span></a>.</p>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><br />
<strong><span style=\"font-size: medium\"></span><span style=\"font-size: medium\">5.6</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: medium\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\">&nbsp;-&nbsp;</span></span></span>Use of Air Inter VA call signs on IVAO and VATSIM networks:<br data-end=\"10789\" data-start=\"10786\" />
Flight plan call signs are no longer automatically recognized. To be called correctly by controllers:</p>

<ul>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">For <strong>Air Inter</strong>: Add to the FPL REMARK section: <strong>OPR/Air Inter</strong></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">For <strong>Air Charter International</strong>: Add to the FPL REMARK section: <strong>OPR/Air Charter International</strong></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">For <strong>Inter Cargo Service</strong>: Add to the FPL&nbsp;REMARK section: <strong>OPR/Inter Cargo Services</strong></li>
</ul>

<h2 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: medium\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: medium\"><br />
<span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\">6-</span></span></strong><span style=\"text-decoration:underline;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\">SUBSTITUTE AIRCRAFT</span></span></span></strong></span><br />
&nbsp;</h2>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\"><strong>6.0&nbsp;</strong></span><strong><span style=\"font-size: medium\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\">-&nbsp;</span></span></strong></span><strong>List of substitute aircraft depending on simulator used.</strong><br />
Not all Air Inter aircraft are represented in all flight simulators. Here is the list of authorized replacement aircraft according to the simulator.<span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\"></span></span><br />
<br />
<strong><span style=\"font-size: medium\">a) FS2004 and FSX:</span></strong></span></p>

<ul>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\">&nbsp;</span></span>All Air Inter aircraft are available on these simulators; no replacement aircraft.<span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\"></span></span></li>
</ul>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><br />
<strong><span style=\"font-size: medium\">b) X-Plane:</span></strong></span></p>

<ul>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\">&nbsp;</span></span>The list of aircraft requiring replacement is not fully known. Until a complete list is available, replacement is at the member’s discretion, prioritizing aircraft similar in size, passenger capacity, and performance to the missing type.<span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\"></span></span></li>
</ul>

